        "original_id": "d9499199-4e8c-5d1a-94bc-d9e66bf7d1b7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: A Leela of Her Own, A League of Their Own, Futurama\n- People: Hank Aaron, Bob Uecker, Tom Kenny\n- Organizations: Fox network, Atlanta Braves, Major League Baseball\n- Roles: voice actors, guest stars, right fielder, senior vice president\n\nFacts:\n- Hank Aaron was born on February 5, 1934.\n- Hank Aaron is nicknamed \"Hammer\" and \"Hammerin' Hank.\"\n- Hank Aaron is a retired American Major League Baseball right fielder.\n- Hank Aaron is the senior vice president of the Atlanta Braves.\n- \"A Leela of Her Own\" is the sixteenth episode of the third season of Futurama.\n- \"A Leela of Her Own\" is an homage to \"A League of Their Own.\"\n- \"A Leela of Her Own\" originally aired in the United States on the Fox network on April 7, 2002.\n- Bob Uecker voiced himself in \"A Leela of Her Own.\"\n- Tom Kenny voiced Abner Doubledeal in \"A Leela of Her Own.\"\n- Hank Aaron guest starred as himself and Hank Aaron XXIV in \"A Leela of Her Own.\"",
